peak to the  committee uh so if he wishes to  we will arrange that meeting this  afternoon  have you put one in yourself a letter  i'm not going to answer that question  but uh  i think technically it would be possible  but it was like the old thing to do  are you surprised at the speed with  which number 10 is moving you've seen a  few of these come and go these events  i'm not surprised by the speed our rules  say should be done as soon as is  reasonable in the circumstances uh when  we held a vote on  theresa may's position  in december 2018  we spoke the evening before and we held  a vote the next day  so you know i suppose it's in line with  recent precedent and i think it's  good for everybody to get these things  out of the way as quickly and efficient  as as possible how long could a contest  actually take if there is one at the end  of it i'm not going to speculate about  leadership elections  we're holding a vote of confidence and  it will take place today and uh you will  have a result this evening  uh  well i i a confidence vote obviously  will provide a clear answer the party  will have confidence in the leadership  or not have confidence in the leadership  that's the question that will be before  my colleagues today  technically it's possible for rules to  be changed but the rule at present is  that there will be a year of a period of  over grace break in terms of foreign  leadership i think my constituents have  been enjoying the jubilee as we all have  i think unless you've got any other  questions of detail  thank you
 

